index 0000000..efa7169
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/tag-folder-record-notes.md
@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+# Native tag folders (Python)
+
+The Python reader exposes `SkpModel.layer_folders` and `Layer.id`,
+`Layer.folder_id`, `Layer.position`. `LayerFolder` records have `id`, `name`,
+`parent_id`, `position`, `hidden`, and `visible_on_new_scenes`. IDs are local to
+one parsed model; names can repeat. The implicit root is not exposed as a folder.
+
+The classic writer exposes `add_layer_folder(name, parent=None, hidden=False,
+visible_on_new_scenes=True)` and `set_layer_folder(layer_handle, folder_handle)`.
+Folder handles are local integers; `None` moves a tag back to the root. Finish
+layers, folders and membership before defining or emitting geometry. Empty
+folders and tags survive. `open_existing()` replay, Python code generation and
+JSON metadata export carry the hierarchy too. With folders present, the writer
+extends its classic container using a newer layer-manager schema; readers must
+support tag folders (SketchUp 2021+). This is not a new VFF geometry writer.
+Without folders the existing writer's format and behavior are unchanged.
+
+## Modern VFF records
+
+Within layer manager `983A`, the flat tag list remains `993A` > `8C3C`.
+`9B3A` contains an implicit `803E` root. Each folder has:
+
+- `DC05` > `DE05`: persistent entity ID.
+- `813E`: UTF-8 name (empty only for the implicit root).
+- `833E`: ordered direct children, each another `803E`.
+- `843E`: direct tag references, each `(u8 byte length, little-endian ID)`.
+- `823E`: current hidden flag.
+- `853E`: hidden-on-new-scenes flag.
+
+A page `7148` records hidden folder IDs in `5971` (numeric tag `0x7159`),
+using the same length-prefixed ID encoding. Python exposes these on
+`Page.hidden_layer_folder_ids`. Existing scene export remains outside the
+classic writer's scope.
+
+## Classic MFC records
+
+The file's **CVersionMap**, rather than just its year or the individual class
+header, determines these versions. Layer-manager schema 7 writes an inline
+implicit root after the active-layer back-reference and before definition
+count. Definitions embed their own layer manager and also need an implicit
+empty root; omitting it can leave a file that our reader accepts but SketchUp
+rejects.
+
+Named folders are `CLayerGroup` objects: entity preamble, UTF-16 name, u32 child
+count and object refs, u32 tag count and layer refs, then visibility. Global
+CLayerGroup version 2 stores a single hidden byte; version 3 adds the
+hidden-on-new-scenes byte. Some older implicit roots omit the PID mask.
+The writer declares version 3, uses native archive slot allocation and includes
+folder slots in all following geometry/tail reference shifts and PID counters.
+
+## Verification
+
+`packages/python/tests/test_tagfolders.py` generates tests on demand. Ordinary
+CI covers byte decoding, duplicate names, malformed IDs, classic round trips,
+replay and Python code generation. Set `OPENSKP_TEST_SKETCHUP_SDK` to a locally
+available SketchUpAPI library for independent checks: SDK-created classic/VFF
+folders, SDK reads of our writer's folder tree and geometry counts, VFF resaves,
+and scene-specific hidden folders. No SDK binary or SDK-produced fixture is
+included. The production parser/writer never loads the SDK.
+
+Cross-language ports are not part of this Python change. Locking and expansion
+state are application-specific and are not written as native SketchUp fields.
